From: krita-wasm-sdk contributors
Subject: [PATCH] compiler settings: do not pass ELF dtags to wasm-ld

Emscripten is UNIX in CMake, but wasm-ld does not accept
--enable-new-dtags. The option also breaks every subsequent try_compile
and produces false-negative feature checks.

Applies to: ECM 6.24.0
Upstream status: local Wasm porting patch, not submitted

diff --git a/kde-modules/KDECompilerSettings.cmake b/kde-modules/KDECompilerSettings.cmake
--- a/kde-modules/KDECompilerSettings.cmake
+++ b/kde-modules/KDECompilerSettings.cmake
@@ -442,7 +442,7 @@
     cmake_policy(SET CMP0063 NEW)
 endif()
 
-if (UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT CYGWIN)
+if (UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT CYGWIN AND NOT EMSCRIPTEN)
     # Enable adding DT_RUNPATH, which means that LD_LIBRARY_PATH takes precedence
     # over the built-in rPath
     set(CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS "-Wl,--enable-new-dtags ${CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS}")
